.TH _CJSON_SET_TYPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
_cjson_set_typed \- path-write back-end (prefer cjson_set macro)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cjson.h>

ccol_retval_t _cjson_set_typed(cjson root, const char *path,
                                cjson_node_type_t type,
                                void *raw, size_t raw_size,
                                bool is_signed, bool raw_is_char_array);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Writes a scalar value to the leaf addressed by path.  The leaf is
created if absent (its immediate parent must already exist).  If the
leaf exists its type is changed unconditionally and any composite
(array, object) resources it previously owned are deep-freed.

type must be one of CJSON_NULL, CJSON_BOOL, CJSON_INTEGER, CJSON_FLOAT,
or CJSON_STRING; any other value (including CJSON_LIST / CJSON_DICTIONARY,
or the internal sentinel cjson_set's own _Generic dispatch produces for a
C type outside its accepted-type list) is rejected with ccol_invalid_args
before the target node is touched.

raw is a void pointer to the C value; raw_size is sizeof the original
C expression.  For string values, raw points to a const char * variable
unless raw_is_char_array is true, in which case raw points directly at
the char[] bytes of a string literal.

For type == CJSON_NULL with raw pointing at a full pointer-sized payload
(raw_size == sizeof(void *), exactly what the cjson_set() macro always
supplies for this type), the pointed-to void * value itself must be NULL;
a non-NULL void * is rejected with ccol_invalid_args rather than being
silently written as CJSON_NULL.  A direct call passing raw == NULL /
raw_size == 0 for a genuine "no payload" null is unaffected by this check.

Escape sequences in path components:
  \e.   -> literal '.' in the key (not a path separator)
  \e\e   -> literal '\e' in the key
A '\e' before any other character is left unchanged.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success            - leaf created or updated.
ccol_invalid_args       - NULL root/path, an empty path or path
                           component (leading, trailing, or
                           consecutive dots), a parent type
                           incompatible with the leaf component, a
                           malformed "#N" index (non-numeric,
                           negative, or bare '#'), type/raw is not
                           one of the accepted scalar forms, or
                           type == CJSON_NULL with a non-NULL
                           void * payload (see above).
ccol_key_not_found      - the parent path, or a syntactically valid
                           but out-of-range list index, is absent.
ccol_not_enough_memory  - allocation failure.
ccol_container_full     - the parent dictionary has already reached
                           its maximum element count (creating a new
                           key only).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_set (macro) (3),
.BR _cjson_get (3)
